From 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ASRock Rack <noreply@asrock.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power_control: don't error-log an absent BeepCode provider

beep() calls xyz.openbmc_project.BeepCode on every power-fail event, but that
interface has no implementation anywhere in the OpenBMC tree -- it is expected
to come from a platform-specific daemon. On a board without one the call always
fails with org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.ServiceUnknown, which sd-bus maps to
EHOSTUNREACH, so every power-off logs

    power-control: beep returned error with async_method_call
                   (ec = No route to host)

That is a missing optional feature, not a fault. Demote just that errno to
debug and leave the error path intact for genuine call failures.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/src/power_control.cpp
+++ b/src/power_control.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include <boost/asio/steady_timer.hpp>
 #include <boost/container/flat_map.hpp>
 #include <boost/container/flat_set.hpp>
+#include <boost/system/errc.hpp>
 #include <gpiod.hpp>
 #include <nlohmann/json.hpp>
 #include <phosphor-logging/lg2.hpp>
@@ -220,6 +221,20 @@
         [](boost::system::error_code ec) {
             if (ec)
             {
+                // xyz.openbmc_project.BeepCode is an optional, platform-
+                // specific provider; no such daemon exists in the OpenBMC
+                // tree, so on a board without one every power-fail beep
+                // resolves to org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.ServiceUnknown,
+                // which sd-bus maps to EHOSTUNREACH ("No route to host").
+                // That is a missing feature, not a fault -- log it at debug
+                // and keep the error path for real call failures.
+                if (ec == boost::system::errc::host_unreachable)
+                {
+                    lg2::debug(
+                        "beep skipped: no BeepCode provider on this platform (ec = {ERROR_MSG})",
+                        "ERROR_MSG", ec.message());
+                    return;
+                }
                 lg2::error(
                     "beep returned error with async_method_call (ec = {ERROR_MSG})",
                     "ERROR_MSG", ec.message());
